```python
import re

# the csharp code
code = '''
// Comment 1
// Comment 2
[AspNetCore.Antiforgery.IAntiforgery]System.IAsyncResult IAntiforgery.GetTokens_object(System.IO.Ports.SerialPort, [0..45] value);  
// assert
Assert.IsNotNull(tokens);
'''

# regular expression to match assert statements
pattern = "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);"

# find matches
matches = re.findall(pattern, code)

# print matches
for match in matches:
    print(match)
```

You need to replace ```code``` with your C# code. The pattern ```Debug.Assert\(.*?\);``` matches all strings that start with "Debug.Assert" and also match anything (```.*?```) between the parentheses (```\(.*?\)```). 

The solution prints only the parts of the code starting with "Debug.Assert" and ends with a semicolon - which include the assert statements with their respective content.--------------------Here is your output:

